# Constitution

Non-negotiable engineering principles for this project. Every spec, plan, and implementation is
evaluated against these. Fill in the placeholders; keep it short and reviewable.

## Stack

See `AGENTS.md` in the repository root (human-owned, `## Stack` section).

## Principles

- [ ] List non-negotiable engineering principles (e.g., API-first, database migrations reviewed,
      feature flags for risky work, accessibility baseline).
- [ ] Git ownership follows the repo topology declared in `AGENTS.md` (`## Git`): in a
      `single-repo` the agent commits atomically per task (Conventional Commits); in a
      `multirepo` the human owns all git operations and the agent never runs git write commands.

## Quality bar

- [ ] Tests required for new behavior; suite must stay green.
- [ ] Lint/formatting must pass before a task is DONE.
- [ ] No secrets in code; no debug output committed.

## Delegation rules

- `architect` analyzes; the `sdd` orchestrator writes `specs/` artifacts.
- `backend-dev` only edits backend code; `react-dev`/`vue-dev` only edit their frontend.
- `tester` and `reviewer` are read-only; their reports drive fixes, they never edit.
